  "core_idea": "Students pursue different goals in learning: developing competence (mastery) or showing it compared with others (performance). Classroom tasks, evaluation and authority shape which goals students adopt.",
  "key_concepts_note": "Use the concepts already stored for this theory in the library (theories.concepts).",
  "when_to_use": [
    "How do classroom practices or grading affect students' goals and motivation?",
    "Are mastery or performance goals linked to deeper learning or cheating?",
    "Typical data: goal orientation surveys (e.g. PALS), observation, interviews."
  ],
  "common_mistakes": [
    "Using only two goals when later work splits them into approach and avoidance.",
    "Treating goals as traits rather than responses to context.",
    "Mixing personal goals and perceived classroom goal structure in one scale."
  ],
